      "hints": [
        "The voltmeter is connected across the 3400 Ω resistor and thermistor, so its 6.0 V reading is not across the 5800 Ω resistor.",
        "Use the 9.6 V supply to find the potential difference across the 5800 Ω resistor, then use V = IR."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Around the complete series loop, the supply e.m.f. equals the sum of potential differences.",
        "The 5800 Ω resistor therefore has V = 9.6 − 6.0 = 3.6 V across it.",
        "Using V = IR, I = 3.6 / 5800 = 6.2 × 10⁻⁴ A."
      ],
      "checking": {
