        "All three resistive components are in series, so they carry the current found in part (a).",
        "Use either the full-loop e.m.f. or the 6.0 V across the 3400 Ω resistor and thermistor."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "The series current is I = 6.2 × 10⁻⁴ A.",
        "Using the full loop, 9.6 = I(3400 + 5800 + R_T).",
        "Rearranging gives R_T = 9.6 / (6.2 × 10⁻⁴) − 3400 − 5800 = 6.3 × 10³ Ω.",
        "Equivalently, use the voltmeter branch: 6.0 = I(3400 + R_T)."
      ],
